<component type="desktop-application">
  <id>com.github.mikacousin.olc.desktop</id>
  <metadata_license>CC0-1.0</metadata_license>
  <project_license>GPL-3.0-or-later</project_license>
  <name>Open Lighting Console</name>
  <summary>Control your lighting shows</summary>
  <developer id="com.github.mikacousin">
    <name>Mika Cousin</name>
  </developer>
  <launchable type="desktop-id">com.github.mikacousin.olc.desktop</launchable>
  <description>
    <p>Open Lighting Console is free software to control lighting for theater and live shows.</p>
    <p>Some features:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Multi-protocol DMX engine (Art-Net, sACN, Enttec DMX USB Pro/Mk2) and HTP DMX-In</li>
      <li>ETC Eos-style command line with Virtual Console and keyboard shortcuts</li>
      <li>Intelligent fixtures, GDTF import, and N-LED scientific color picker (CIE 1931 xy, Lee/Rosco gels)</li>
      <li>USITT ASCII and ETC Eos show import and export</li>
      <li>Patch management and passive real-time DMX Outputs monitor</li>
      <li>Main Playback with Tracking, Move In Black (MIB), and per-family IFCB timings</li>
      <li>IFCB Palettes, Presets, and Parametric Effects engine</li>
      <li>Ordered Groups, configurable multi-page Faders, and Curves editor</li>
      <li>Track channels view, Live Summary+ tiles, and hybrid expandable Table view</li>
      <li>Virtual Console with easy MIDI learn and bidirectional OSC / OSCQuery / TouchOSC templates</li>
    </ul>
  </description>
  <releases>
    <release version="0.11.1.beta" date="2026-10-07">
      <description>
        <p>This release introduces dynamic hot-configuration of DMX universes without restarts, multi-notebook tab management with drag-and-drop, an interactive undo history tab, a massive core action refactoring for headless operation, and major CPU performance optimizations in olc-monitor.</p>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.10.3.beta" date="2026-05-31">
      <description>
        <p>This release introduces a major architectural overhaul centered around the new CoreEngine, brings visual upgrades to cue playback, introduces new companion utilities, and resolves key stability and hardware compatibility bugs.</p>
      </description>
    </release>
  </releases>
